5. Convert extracted information into structured class events.
6. Identify ambiguous or incomplete fields.
7. Display a timetable preview.
8. Allow individual corrections.
9. Detect overlaps and duplicate events.
10. Save only after user confirmation.

The parser should attempt to identify:
- Weekdays
- Subjects
- Course codes
- Start and end times
- Classroom locations
- Faculty details, if available
- Rotating timetable patterns, if identifiable

Do not assume that every PDF follows the same layout.

If extraction is unreliable, explain the problem and offer manual entry.

## E. Manual timetable management

